 ## Overview
-Renders a single view of a 3D volume by generating rays, sampling density via `grid_sample`, and accumulating attenuation [S1, unofficial]. It supports tiling to manage memory usage for large images [S1, unofficial]. Unlike [Fixed Step Ray Marching](3136-fixed-step-ray-marching.md) which may iterate sequentially, this method leverages batched tensor operations for sampling while using tiling to handle memory constraints that would otherwise cause out-of-memory errors in dense volume rendering [S1, unofficial].
+Renders a single view of a 3D volume by generating rays, sampling density via grid sampling, and accumulating attenuation [S1, unofficial]. It supports tiling to manage memory usage for large images [S1, unofficial]. It differs from [Voxel Ray Marching with Traversal Order Optimization](1251-voxel-ray-marching-with-traversal-order-optimization.md) by using dense grid sampling (e.g., `grid_sample`) rather than sparse voxel traversal, and by explicitly tiling the image plane to bound peak memory usage [S1, unofficial].
 
